.SH EXAMPLES
Create two identities:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ init me \-\-next\-out \- | age \-p > me\-next.key.age
writ init alice \-\-next\-out alice\-next.key
.fi
.RE
.PP
Name alice, and let her log in to nas:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ name \-i me alice alice >> bundle.writ
writ grant \-i me 'me alice' '(ssh nas)' >> bundle.writ
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check, as nas would:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ check \-\-as me alice '(ssh nas)' < bundle.writ
.fi
.RE
.SH STANDARDS
SLH\-DSA (FIPS 205), ML\-DSA (FIPS 204), Ed25519 (RFC 8032), SHA\-3 and SHAKE (FIPS 202), bech32m (BIP 350). The exact formats are in SPEC.md in the writ source.
